{"base_rate":0.3963254593175853,"brier":0.12832401574803148,"bss":0.46364404117477687,"bss_hi":0.5452957177601765,"bss_lo":0.3743803126617573,"chart":{"base":[404.6,117.8],"fp":[304.5,269.0],"lead":"62,252 272,224.9 482,171.6 692,97.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.46 — higher than 87% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +9pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 51% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 4%; promised 98% → rained 84%"},"rel":"62,450.4 169.1,341.5 514.7,157.4 682.5,103.4"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07969816272965871,"ess":410.631243845627,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Stuttgart</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Stuttgart rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSTUTTGART-SCHNARRENBERG, 5.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.46, ranked 28 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(12&ndash;66) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>277</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>100</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>168</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Stuttgart</b> <span class=\"muted\">Germany</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;40% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 40% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.46</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>12&ndash;66\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Stuttgart &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Stuttgart\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 82.0366,338.32 165.11948051948053,235.45454545454544 273.32640000000004,124.65200000000067 357.3750769230769,46.0 406.6689285714285,18.0 406.6689285714285,31.0 357.3750769230769,107.60000000000002 273.32640000000004,202.42666666666665 165.11948051948053,306.3636363636364 82.0366,374.72 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"237.73753280839895\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"237.73753280839895\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,368.85920577617327 82.0366,320.12 165.11948051948053,221.27272727272728 273.32640000000004,149.04 357.3750769230769,90.80000000000001 406.6689285714285,76.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 277 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"368.85920577617327\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 100 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"82.0366\" cy=\"320.12\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"165.11948051948053\" cy=\"221.27272727272728\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"273.32640000000004\" cy=\"149.04\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"357.3750769230769\" cy=\"90.80000000000001\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 168 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.6689285714285\" cy=\"76.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Stuttgart the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.57) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.35).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.352</td><td class='num'>8.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.374</td><td class='num'>10.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.530</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.569</td><td class='num'>4.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":48.78232,"lon":9.17702,"n":762,"n_cities":216,"name":"Stuttgart","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":277,"obs":0.036101083032490974,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.06790000000000002,"n":100,"obs":0.17,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.3025974025974026,"n":77,"obs":0.44155844155844154,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.6082666666666668,"n":75,"obs":0.64,"sig":false},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8456923076923076,"n":65,"obs":0.8,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.984940476190476,"n":168,"obs":0.8392857142857143,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.5,"provisional":false,"rank":28,"rank_hi":66.02499999999998,"rank_lo":11.975000000000001,"reliability":0.008747688265350426,"resolution":0.1171036677738673,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"stuttgart","station":"STUTTGART-SCHNARRENBERG","timezone":"Europe/Berlin"}